pendently query live `refs/heads/research/post-v1`; local HEAD, tracking HEAD and live remote HEAD must equal the exact accepted adoption endpoint with `0/0`. Default remote HEAD is not a substitute. Required remote verification unavailable means U/BLOCK.\n7. Reauthenticate the finally accepted substantive state at activation. Resolve every change between C6's dated observations, integration author/review boundaries, adoption/publication and activation through exact separately authorized evidence. No unresolved substantive drift, affecting contradiction, required historical D premise, missing anchor or unknown applicability may remain. Operational/ignored mutations require claim-scoped assessment; neither blanket blocking nor blanket harmlessness is permitted. No undocumented interval continuity is inferred from equal endpoints.\n8. Only a separate explicit external activation authority may issue an exact activation artifact/receipt after these prerequisites. Independently authenticate that artifact and its durable location before reliance. The receipt cannot accept itself. Its resulting identity must be externally bound by the authorized issuing/accepting record and carried into the accepted continuation checkpoint/gate through a separately authorized transition. Do not require a commit to contain its own hash or a receipt to contain its own final digest. No circular publication or effectiveness proof is allowed.\n\n## Required later receipt fields and bindings\n\nThe exact future receipt must include:\n\n- Unique activation ID, schema revision, issuer/task/session and exact authorizing record; authenticated issuance timestamp and ordering.\n- C6 and complete verdict identities, integration package/freeze/canonical delta identities, complete independent integration verdict and explicit acceptance/durable-location records.\n- Exact accepted adoption commit, parent(s), full tree, branch/upstream/origin/refspecs, raw index/entries/stages, complete material boundary an